Embedded GNU GRUB 2.12 Windows BIOS tools
=======================================

The embedded grub-fstest.exe and i386-pc files come from the official GNU release:
https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/grub/grub-2.12-for-windows.zip
https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/grub/grub-2.12-for-windows.zip.sig

The detached signature was verified against the release key fingerprint:
BE5C 2320 9ACD DACE B20D B0A2 8C81 89F1 988C 2166
Published by the maintainer in the official release announcement:
https://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/grub-devel/2023-12/msg00052.html

SHA256 (official ZIP):
e98bf808fcb6836a7e50d0f9483900116b28c46c0b9743cc956e314a7fdea9bd
The official Windows mkimage does not support XZ compression. The installer
build instead cross-compiles the unmodified GNU GRUB 2.12 image utility with
static, threadless liblzma, retaining Windows XP support and system DLLs only.
This permits BIOS installation in small legacy embedding areas. It does not
change the BIOS modules or Debian's signed EFI loaders.

SHA256 (GNU GRUB 2.12 source tar.xz):
f3c97391f7c4eaa677a78e090c7e97e6dc47b16f655f04683ebd37bef7fe0faa
SHA256 (XZ 5.8.1 source tar.xz):
0b54f79df85912504de0b14aec7971e3f964491af1812d83447005807513cd9e
XZ source (Debian mirror of the upstream archive):
https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/x/xz-utils/xz-utils_5.8.1.orig.tar.xz
https://github.com/tukaani-project/xz/releases/tag/v5.8.1
liblzma is distributed under the Zero-Clause BSD license (0BSD):
https://github.com/tukaani-project/xz/blob/v5.8.1/COPYING

The installer build downloads the release ZIP from GNU's kernel.org mirror:
https://mirrors.kernel.org/gnu/grub/grub-2.12-for-windows.zip
It verifies the pinned ZIP and source SHA256 values before compiling/embedding
the tools. See installer/build-windows-grub for the complete build commands.
These build inputs are not stored in the repository.
The ISO distributes them only inside slax-install.exe, without loose Windows
utilities. During BIOS installation, matching i386-pc runtime modules are copied
to the new slax/boot/grub directory; these run in BIOS GRUB, not in Windows.
Debugger helpers, EFI platforms, fonts, locales and other utilities are omitted.
Slax supplies Debian's signed shim and GRUB EFI loaders separately.
The Slax media bundles those loaders in slax/boot/EFI/BOOT. These BIOS tools
are used by the native installer. Its build verifies and embeds grub-mkimage.exe,
grub-fstest.exe and matching modules so helpers are never executed from an
untrusted ISO. The filesystem verifier checks actual access and compares the
copied boot files before replacing any BIOS boot record.
The embedded utility builds a BIOS core; the native engine installs it only
within the explicitly approved BIOS boot area.
These tools and the native installer require only Windows system DLLs.
The native application targets XP onward and requests administrator access.
It does not require VBScript, WMI, PowerShell or additional runtime DLLs.

License: GNU GPL version 3 or later, reproduced in COPYING.windows-grub.
The corresponding unmodified source code is available from GNU:
https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/grub/grub-2.12.tar.xz
